<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices -Nov 8.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices -Nov 8.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>International prices for milling and Durum wheat were unchanged to slightly firmer, while the Australian dollar was weaker, the Austalian Wheat Board (AWB) said. Prices, FOB, in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		    ASW 10 pct		   No 1 DURUM</p>
<p>		    Delivered Port	     Delivered Port</p>
<p>Queensland</p>
<p>    Brisbane	n/a</p>
<p>    Gladstone     n/a</p>
<p>    Mackay	  n/a</p>
<p>New South Wales</p>
<p>    Newcastle     126.75			   n/a</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   127.75</p>
<p>Victoria</p>
<p>    Geelong	 128.00</p>
<p>    Portland	128.75</p>
<p>South Australia</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide 128.75			   n/a</p>
<p>    Port Giles    129.50</p>
<p>Port Lincoln  131.00</p>
<p>    Port Pirie    125.50</p>
<p>    Thevenard     126.00</p>
<p>    Wallaroo	127.25</p>
<p>Western Australia</p>
<p>    Albany	  134.25</p>
<p>    Esperance     132.75</p>
<p>    Fremantle     137.00</p>
<p>    Geraldton     134.00</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1996/97 harvest. Offer valid until 4.30 p.m. Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
